# Inline custom node (no C++ file needed): a few lines with {placeholders}
# substituted at build. Adds {num0} degrees to the target object's yaw.
#
# `desc` says what the NODE does; `tip0` / `tip_string` say what each PARAMETER
# does. The editor shows desc when you hover the node and a tip when you hover
# that widget, and both go into the AI generator's catalog - so writing them is
# how a project's own node stops needing a person to explain it.
title = Spin By
category = Custom
desc = Turns an object a fixed number of degrees about the world Y axis, once per exec. A one-shot: for something that turns continuously use the built-in Spin Object, which the game integrates itself.
string = object
tip_string = The object to turn. Empty = the object owning this graph.
num0 = Degrees
tip0 = How far to turn, in degrees. Negative turns the other way; each exec adds to the last, so firing it twice turns twice as far.
---
ctx.objects[{obj}].data.rotation[1] += {num0};
ctx.objects[{obj}].dirty = true;
